description: Ask for missing product details before adding items or rules
alwaysApply: true
---

# Catalog Change Intake

- Do not invent missing product behavior when adding a new log item or a new rule.
- For a new log item, confirm:
  - name
  - why it matters
  - fields to capture
  - allowed values
  - when users should log it
  - whether it affects trends, summaries, reminders, or warnings
  - one realistic example entry
- For a new rule, confirm:
  - rule name
  - trigger condition
  - time window
  - required user or cat context
  - user-facing output
  - severity
  - exceptions or edge cases
- If required information is missing, ask follow-up questions before editing schema, UI, or logic.
- Update `docs/log-catalog.md` or `docs/rule-catalog.md` before implementation.
